Round complete. Both deliverable files are written (`impl/d1_pow2.c` via the impl symlink, and the appended Round d1_r2 section in `strategies/d1_pow2.md`); the other modified strategy files belong to rivals working concurrently.

**What changed this round.** Two techniques, both aimed at the Ice Lake scoring node's port-5 bottleneck (every 512-bit shuffle there competes with an FMA unit — the reason my r1 code degraded 1.54× cross-machine while shuffle-free rivals degraded 1.32×):

1. **Across-batch SoA chain path, taken openly from d1_batchlane** — groups of 8 transforms in zmm lanes, one 8×8 transpose per group per chain, zero shuffles per step, gated at L≤2048 (at 16384 it measured 2× *slower* than my per-transform blocking, so the gate is load-bearing). Batched chained cells: 32: 0.064→0.032, 64: 0.116→0.062, 128: 0.233→0.146 µs — this flips the one cell where a library beat me (fftw custom_soa at L=32).
2. **Blocked split-complex radix-8 engine for L≥128** — the stride-1 stage writes [8 re | 8 im] blocks for free (same transpose cost either way), all middle stages are zero-shuffle vertical FMA, the final re-interleaves with the map fused in split form. Three failed intermediate designs are recorded with their numbers (plane format lost 42% to stream-count blowup; a dedicated conversion stage lost 24%; a second scratch buffer lost 20% at the L1 boundary — that one masqueraded as a kernel problem until I rebuilt the AoS reference on equal buffers). Chained wins: 128 chain 0.231→0.173, 1024 2.17→1.72, 4096 10.8→9.2, 16384 49.7→41.7; non-chained at wallaby parity, with the ICX shuffle relief as the scoring-node bet. Also logged: llvm-mca's icelake-server model assumes one 512-bit FMA unit and cannot judge p0/p5 balance on the Gold 6326.

All 24 graded pow2 cells pass (single-call rel L2 ≤ 3.4e-16, worst chain gate 4.5e-12 vs 1e-10), remainder batches and repeatability verified, no slurm jobs submitted.

**One-liner:** Blocked split-complex radix-8 Stockham (zero-shuffle middle stages) + batchlane-style SoA batch chains; wallaby best at m=1: 0.012/0.012 (L=32), 0.073/0.089 (128), 1.01/1.49 (1024), 6.68/8.91 (4096), 27.0/37.1 µs (16384), chained down 13–50% everywhere; rel L2 ≤ 3.4e-16 single-call, worst chain 4.5e-12.
